/* ================================================================
   Poggy theme skin: poggy_skillcheck (ui/index.html)

   Covers the skill check's chrome: the key label in the ring, the
   streak counter, and the hit flashes (good = success, great = accent,
   fail = danger) and the fail tint.

   Left alone on purpose: the ring itself. It is a <canvas> painted by
   skillcheck.js with fixed colours (grey track, white hit zone, gold
   great zone, red needle, dark hub), which CSS cannot reach. The zone
   colours are the game's meaning (hit here, hit here for a great), so
   they stay as they are either way. The heavy black drop shadow round
   the ring stays too: it is a shadow, black on every theme.

   The ring is always dark (canvas + black shadow), so the streak counter
   gets a small chip of its own, drawn with a box-shadow spread so nothing
   moves; text in the theme's colour would vanish into the ring on Ledger.
   ================================================================ */

html.pg-themed #skillcheck-key {
    background: var(--pg-popup-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--pg-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--pg-radius-sm);
    box-shadow: var(--pg-shadow);
    color: var(--pg-text);
    font-family: var(--pg-font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-shadow: none;
}

html.pg-themed #skillcheck-streak {
    font-family: var(--pg-font-body);
    color: var(--pg-text-soft);
    text-shadow: none;
    background: var(--pg-raise);
    box-shadow:
        0 0 0 3px var(--pg-raise),
        0 0 0 4px var(--pg-border);
}
html.pg-themed #skillcheck-streak:empty {
    background: none;
    box-shadow: none;
}

html.pg-themed #skillcheck-flash.flash-good  { box-shadow: inset 0 0 40px rgba(var(--pg-success-rgb), 0.45); }
html.pg-themed #skillcheck-flash.flash-great { box-shadow: inset 0 0 40px rgba(var(--pg-accent-rgb), 0.55); }
html.pg-themed #skillcheck-flash.flash-fail  { box-shadow: inset 0 0 60px rgba(var(--pg-danger-rgb), 0.60); }

html.pg-themed #skillcheck-fail-tint {
    background: radial-gradient(circle,
        rgba(var(--pg-danger-rgb), 0.35) 0%,
        rgba(var(--pg-danger-rgb), 0.18) 70%,
        transparent 100%);
}
